title: Spørsmål til NHN
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Open questions from the project team. Each one either blocks a feature from being useful or decides how it should be finished. Answers can be written straight into this tiddler.

# ''Service owners'' — [[Tjenesteeiere]] [service owners] is built, but no service has a `tjenesteeier` [service owner] yet. Who supplies the list of services → owners (a spreadsheet paste is enough), and when? Until then the owner column in the ToDo lists and the owner grouping under //Tjenester// [services] are empty.
# ''Tag cleanup'' — may we normalise the spelling and casing drift in tags (`Ekstern tjeneste` [external service] / `Ekstern Tjeneste`, `Leveranse` [delivery] / `leveranse`, …), and which tag families first? [[Anomalier]] [anomalies] shows every affected tiddler. This is the one change that rewrites your data, so we want sign-off per class.
# ''Other anomalies'' — [[Anomalier]] also lists self-tagging, service-type tags on monthly reviews, multi-parent objectives, duplicated year versions, ambiguous Målsetting [objective] / Resultat [key result] tiddlers, and 31 tiddlers where a bullet list has no blank line before it (so the bullets show as literal `*` text — e.g. [[02 Styringsrapport DHP februar 2025]] [governance report, February 2025]). Fix these, leave them, or fix some? The blank-line one is mechanical and we can run it in bulk with your approval.
# ''Archiving'' — [[Arkiv]] [archive] hides prior years behind an `Arkiv` tag, reversibly, without deleting anything. Is that enough, or should old years leave the live wiki entirely (a separate read-only archive wiki)?
# ''Business-review rules'' — the ToDo list counts a review as done only if its text differs from the template and from last month's review. Is an exact comparison right, or should a review that is a near-copy be flagged too? And should `Forretningsmessig endring` [business change, i.e. severity] be required on a new review? 84% of existing reviews lack it, so we made it optional.
# ''Which services'' — the ToDo lists default to services that reported at least once this year (43 of 60), with //Alle tjenester// [all services] as a toggle. Is that the right default, or should the list of services expected to report be maintained explicitly?
# ''Permalink base'' — exported URLs use `https://tiddlywiki.plattform.nhn.no/#…`. Confirm this is the address readers should be given.
# ''Access control'' (§3.8) — editors vs readers must be enforced in front of the Node.js server (AD/OIDC proxy), not in the plugin. Who owns the hosting, and is an auth proxy available on that platform?
# ''Deployment'' — how do you want the plugins delivered: as plugin folders dropped into the existing Node.js wiki, or as a rebuilt wiki? And who installs updates?
